WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:19.290
X seventeen is the First Napoleon Point of triangle A B C: by Napoleon's theorem, the centroids Nap sub a, Nap sub b, and Nap sub c of the three outward equilateral triangles erected on sides B C, C A, and A B always form an equilateral triangle, and the lines joining A, B, and C to those three centers concur at X seventeen.

2
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:30.183
Its trilinear coordinates shift the phase to pi over six: cosecant of A plus pi over six, to cosecant of B plus pi over six, to cosecant of C plus pi over six.

3
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:39.800
On the central lines layer, X seventeen lies on line X three X thirteen, line X four X fifteen, line X five X fourteen, and line X six X eighteen.

4
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:50.060
X seventeen lies on the Kiepert hyperbola at angle plus thirty degrees, is the isogonal conjugate of X sixty-one, and pairs with the Second Napoleon Point X eighteen.
